  "_capture": {
    "note": "Captured from real Codex sessions by a temporary command-hook probe plugin, then sanitised. Do not hand-edit; re-capture instead. Two captures: codex-cli 0.154.0 on 2026-09-23 gave everything not listed under `captures[1].gave`; a second, interactive one (codex-tui) on codex-cli 0.165.0 on 2026-10-27 added Interrupt, SubagentStart, SubagentStop, PreToolUse:spawn and the esc, spawn and parallel sequences. envKeys are the first capture's hook environment; the second ran from a login shell and inherited all of it, so its names are not kept. Keys are exactly as captured. Kept verbatim: hook_event_name, permission_mode, source, tool_name, model, reason, trigger, stop_hook_active, agent_type. Ids are stable fakes in the captured format, so events that shared an id still share one — including the uuid inside a transcript path. cwd and every path are moved under a fake root; apply_patch keeps its directive lines with remapped paths, and its hunk bodies are replaced. Command text, every other tool_input value (a PermissionRequest's description; the spawn call's task_name, fork_turns and message), tool responses, the prompt and the assistant messages are replaced by markers. A sequence's afterMs is measured from its first record by the probe's own clock, and records are in the order the probe appended them: parallel hooks can disagree by a millisecond.",
