    "settles": [
      "PermissionRequest carries tool_name and tool_input but no tool_use_id.",
      "PreToolUse fires BEFORE PermissionRequest for the same call.",
      "apply_patch carries ABSOLUTE paths in its directives.",
      "The first capture's one permission was answered by an automatic reviewer: no human, and the next event arrived ~11.9s later with no PostToolUse for the requested call — which is why the Codex dwell is 30s, not 5s.",
      "Esc at an approval prompt sends Interrupt (~4.5s after the PermissionRequest here) and nothing else: no PostToolUse for the requested call and no Stop. Interrupt carries the root's session_id and turn_id and no agent_id.",
      "A request a human approved got its PostToolUse 3.3s later, with the PreToolUse's tool_use_id (not kept as a sequence).",
      "A Bash PermissionRequest's tool_input carries a description its PreToolUse does not.",
      "A spawned subagent shares the root's session_id, runs its own turn_id, and is named by agent_id; its agent_type was \"default\". SubagentStart's transcript_path is the subagent's own rollout; SubagentStop's is the root's, with the subagent's in agent_transcript_path.",
      "SubagentStop adds agent_transcript_path, stop_hook_active and last_assistant_message, and no success or failure field.",
      "The spawn tool is collaborationspawn_agent, its tool_use_id is call_<32 hex> rather than exec-<uuid>, and its PostToolUse arrives before SubagentStart (~1.0s): the call does not stay open while the subagent runs.",
      "Tool calls run in parallel: three PreToolUse within 42 ms, and their PostToolUse arrive in a different order, matched to their calls only by tool_use_id.",
      "No captured tool event carries agent_id: the one captured subagent ran no tool, so a subagent's own tool call is still declared, not captured (declared.json)."
    ],
